.TH NDICLIENT 1 "October 2026" "ndiclient 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ndiclient \- command line NDI video receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ndiclient
.br
.B ndiclient
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen ]
.I device-name
.RI [ stream-name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ndiclient
finds an NDI source on the network and shows its video in a desktop window
or fullscreen.
.PP
Without arguments, it discovers sources for 5 seconds, prints the full NDI
name of each one and exits.
.PP
With arguments, it shows the source named
.IR device-name " (" stream-name ).
The device name matches ignoring case; the stream name must match exactly.
Without a stream name, the first stream discovered on the device is shown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Cover the whole screen instead of opening a 1280x720 window, and hide the
mouse cursor. May appear anywhere among the arguments.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR F11 ", " F
Switch between window and fullscreen.
.TP
.B Escape
Quit. Closing the window also quits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, also when listing finds no sources.
.TP
.B 1
No matching source was found within 10 seconds, or another error occurred.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
When run over SSH, export the desktop session first, for example
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/$(id \-u)
and
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland\-0 .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ndiclient
List the NDI sources on the network.
.TP
.B ndiclient STUDIO \(dqOBS PGM\(dq
Show the source
.BR "STUDIO (OBS PGM)" .
.TP
.B ndiclient \-\-fullscreen STUDIO
Show the first stream of device STUDIO fullscreen.
